# Template for /etc/dyx3/ros.env — read by dyx3-ros, dyx3-recorder, dyx3-rtk and dyx3-spray-watchdog. Created once by the installer; an upgrade never
# overwrites it.
#
# REQUIRED. The fleet's ROS domain is 42 (decided in the 2026-10-09 production review). Change it only if another ROS graph on the
# same network already uses 42. The launchers refuse to start while it is unset (they never guess), and a fresh install refuses
# to start without it.
ROS_DOMAIN_ID=42
#
# DDS scoping (architecture 4.4 "DDS scoped to eth0"), DECIDED 2026-10-10: loopback-only. The ROS graph is local to the Jetson, and
# PX4 reaches it only through the XRCE agent on this host (PX4 UXRCE_DDS_PTCFG=1, a localhost participant, with UXRCE_DDS_DOM_ID equal to
# ROS_DOMAIN_ID above). Loopback-only is stricter than an eth0 whitelist and survives an unplugged FCU cable. Remove this line only on a
# bench that needs a second machine on the graph. The launchers turn it into ROS_LOCALHOST_ONLY=1 (deployment/scripts/dyx3-env.sh).
#
# An upgrade never overwrites this file: a rover installed before this default must add the next line by hand once.
DYX3_ROS_LOCALHOST_ONLY=1
